<article class="env-lemma" id="07RW">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/07RW">Lemma <span data-tag="07RW">15.7.5</span>.</a> With $A, A', B, B', C, C', D, D', I$ as in Situation <a href="/tag/08KK" data-tag="08KK">15.7.1</a>. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
Let $(N, M', \varphi )$ be an object of $\text{Mod}_ D \times _{\text{Mod}_ C} \text{Mod}_{C'}$. If $M'$ is flat over $A'$ and $N$ is flat over $B$, then $N' = N \times _{\varphi , M} M'$ is flat over $B'$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
If $L'$ is a $D'$-module flat over $B'$, then $L' = (L \otimes _{D'} D) \times _{(L \otimes _{D'} C)} (L \otimes _{D'} C')$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
The category of $D'$-modules flat over $B'$ is equivalent to the categories of objects $(N, M', \varphi )$ of $\text{Mod}_ D \times _{\text{Mod}_ C} \text{Mod}_{C'}$ with $N$ flat over $B$ and $M'$ flat over $A'$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Part (1) follows from part (1) of Lemma <a href="/tag/0D2I" data-tag="0D2I">15.6.8</a>. 
    <p>
      Part (2) follows from part (2) of Lemma <a href="/tag/0D2I" data-tag="0D2I">15.6.8</a> using that $L' \otimes _{D'} D = L' \otimes _{B'} B$, $L' \otimes _{D'} C' = L' \otimes _{B'} A'$, and $L' \otimes _{D'} C = L' \otimes _{B'} A$, see discussion in Situation <a href="/tag/08KK" data-tag="08KK">15.7.1</a>. 
    <p>
      Part (3) is an immediate consequence of (1) and (2). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>